  <constraints>
    <constraint type="cost">This step has zero API cost. It is a pure shell command running on EC2. Execution time is approximately 2 seconds.</constraint>
    <constraint type="output-format">Output MUST be one line per file in STATUS\tFILENAME format. git diff --name-status naturally produces this (e.g., M\tsrc/app.tsx). The find fallback must format output to match (map found files to A\tFILENAME).</constraint>
    <constraint type="exclusions">Must exclude node_modules/, .git/, and knowledge/ directories from the diff output. These directories contain either third-party code, version control metadata, or compiled knowledge (which would create circular compilation).</constraint>
    <constraint type="idempotency">The .mycelium/last-compile-marker must only be updated AFTER successful diff extraction. If the step fails, the marker remains unchanged so the next run picks up all changes since the last successful compile.</constraint>
    <constraint type="first-run">On first-ever compilation, there may be no git history and no marker file. The command must handle both cases gracefully — either producing a complete diff or treating all files as new (A status).</constraint>
  </constraints>

